THE CLASS THIS EXISTS FOR. Six ADR-0017 artifacts were closed `done` on "N
tests, 100% coverage" while having no production caller -- infer_summary,
is_field_tainted, select_ddg_targets and peers. Every reference to them was
PROSE: an ADR section, a sibling docstring, a test docstring. Each parsed,
linted, and sat at 100% coverage held there by its own tests. R16 is satisfied
by written triggers today; this is the executable one.

CALLERS, NOT SEEDS -- why this version works where the filed one was refused.
dead-code-maybe asks "is this reachable from the production seed set", and the
seeds are entrypoints PLUS exported public API, so a public function with zero
in-repo callers can never be flagged. That is exactly the shape this family
has. Measured on that question the gate caught 3 of its own 6 motivating
examples and would have fired ~1,747 times on day one; the owner refused it.
Asking "does every DIRECT CALLER live in a test module" flags all three it used
to miss AND spares the control -- load_function_summaries, the one member
genuinely fixed by PR #197, is correctly absent. Both pinned as tests.

THE DEMOTION ARM IS THE GATE, and every case in it was a live false positive
before it was a test. Three reference mechanisms are invisible to a
calls/instantiates edge set:

  cmd_slice                `p_slice.set_defaults(func=cmd_slice)` -- a VALUE
                           BINDING, and cmd_slice is the entry point of
                           `hypergumbo slice`
  link_decorator_dispatch  carries @register_linker(...); the first cut indexed
                           the DECORATOR's name and left the REGISTERED
                           function gated
  _install_rust_analyzer_with_bug06_gate
                           referenced as `cli_mod._install_...` in its OWN
                           module, which the first cut excluded

Demotion removes 472 of 789: 160 registry-decorated (@register_analyzer 116,
@register_linker 44), 79 production-referenced, 27 dispatch-bound, 2 used as
decorators, 204 methods. GATED COHORT: 317.

A PRIOR MEASUREMENT IS REFUTED AND THE CORRECTION IS PINNED. A 2026-08-30 note
called 101 analyze_<lang> wrappers "*** DEAD ***" after spot-checking
analyze_scheme and finding "ZERO production references ... a shim nothing in
production names". True, and irrelevant: scheme.py:373 carries
@register_analyzer("scheme") on the line directly above the def, and 125
modules register their entry point that way. The gate demotes all of them.

METHODS ARE COUNTED, NEVER GATED, and the reason is measured. A method's
call-graph identity is its SHORT name, so Store.add cannot be told from set.add
and Pattern.matches scores hundreds of hits off re's .matches. Deciding a
method needs receiver typing (INV-linub, open). Gating ~200 unadjudicable rows
would make the baseline the rubber stamp the owner's own ruling forbids.

PARSED, NEVER GREPPED. A grep proxy once scored infer_summary as having one
production reference; it was a COMMENT reading "infer_summary still has zero
production callers". Prose about deadness counted as evidence of life. The
index collects ast.Name loads and ast.Attribute accesses, with a test asserting
a name in a comment or docstring is not a reference.

NOT A PER-PR GATE, because the cost was measured: a self-map takes 13m40s and
236MB. It runs in the full-suite reusing the /tmp/self-tree.json the WI-jigup
ratchet already builds, so it costs seconds. Missing map or baseline exits 2 --
infrastructure, warn and continue, per the mypy ratchet's contract. In the
workflow `|| rc=$?` is load-bearing: Actions runs bash -e, so a bare invocation
would abort before the exit-2 branch could fire.

The baseline key is `path::name` and omits the line span on purpose: an
id-keyed baseline churns on every edit that moves a line, producing a diff
nobody reads -- which is how a ratchet becomes a rubber stamp.

Tests: 41, 100% coverage on the new module. 1759 passed, mypy ratchet clean.

